cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on the experiments, please cite both the software release and the paper below."
title: "v2x_adversarial_sensing: honest, reproducible release of the Dual-Stream Phase-Aware Inception-Time CNN for adversarially robust V2X spectrum sensing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dhankhar"
    given-names: "Parveen"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Vaish College of Engineering, Rohtak, India"
  - family-names: "Vats"
    given-names: "Davesh"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Vaish College of Engineering, Rohtak, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Daveshvats/v2x_adversarial_sensing"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research artifact for the ICE2CT-2026 paper "Dual-Stream
  Phase-Aware Inception-Time CNN for Adversarially Robust Spectrum Sensing in
  V2X Networks". Contains the exact pipeline behind the paper's Tables II/III/V:
  a synthetic V2X dataset generator (LTE / WiFi / V2X-PC5 / Noise, Rayleigh
  fading), the 86,052-parameter Dual-Stream Inception-Time CNN trained with
  TF-CutMix, FGSM/PGD/APGD/FAB/Square adversarial evaluation, a corrected
  metrics module (robust accuracy and conditional ASR), a one-command
  reproduction harness, and a full honesty audit (AUDIT.md) that reconciles
  every legacy result file in the repository, including one that is marked
  invalid and not citable. Runs on CPU only.
keywords:
  - "spectrum sensing"
  - "V2X"
  - "C-V2X"
  - "adversarial machine learning"
  - "adversarial robustness"
  - "wireless security"
  - "deep learning"
  - "PyTorch"
  - "reproducibility"
